    "turn_text": "military, I thought was the best way that I could combine all those things and see if I had what it took, not only to do, you know, more than three pullups, but stand in front of, you know, 40 Marines, most of whom were older than me and lead them in a very difficult environment. And that was the best decision I ever made. Certainly an odd decision. Some of my peers, I think, were surprised that I did it. I mean, you know, 2005, when I went to Oxford County School, the bottom really fell out of the country in Iraq. You know, we had this marimosque bombing shortly thereafter. You know, it was really, things are really going bad. You know, this was the, and Petraeus, you know, pre-stirge was just getting savaged in the media. And so this was not like a popular war nor a popular Princeton decision to join the Marine Corps, but I loved it. Sorry, I went on here, but let me tell one more story.",
