    "turn_idx": 74,
    "turn_text": "maybe I'm now in the minority on this, but I just think the fundamentals of a robust military deterrent combined with strong allies and a clear moral leadership of the free world is the best recipe for security, safety, and prosperity going forward. And the fact is now for the first time since Reagan defeated the Soviet Union, we find ourselves in a new Cold War with the communist adversary in the form of the Chinese Communist Party. And to me, that is the struggle of our generation. And it is a struggle that the Republican Party needs to confront head on. And I think it also presents an opportunity to lay a bipartisan foundation for US foreign policy. So if I were advising, the Republican Party on where to go. Those would be three things that I would add to the debate. And I think that those are the right things to focus on from a policy perspective. And ultimately, they'll be the best things politically as well.",
