    "turn_text": "people want authenticity more than anything else. And so for me, I like to joke around. I think it's important to have a sense of humor. And so I always tell people to take the mission, but not yourself too seriously. And having a sense of humor about things is a great survival strategy going forward. Oh, and let me just add one final thing. This ties back until a party time and showing up early. Get up early and spend the first hour of your day you know, after you've done your, your morning prayer, writing, I have an app on my computer called freedom that turns off internet in every single morning for the past six years, almost without fail. It made me the deception when I was on my honeymoon. I have spent the first hour of my day thinking and writing, even when I'm not working on writing projects, it's helpful. And just having that time is the best way to stay on offense before the day puts you on defense. So That's all of the wisdom I've learned in 36 years into four cheesy aphorisms, I guess.",
